        "text": "Answers\n1.I Yes, but it is recommended to deploy it in a container.\n2.I Technically, it is feasible, but it is not a best practice. Database failure will bring both\nmicroservices down.\n3.I Docker Compose is a tool for deploying and running container applications using a\nYAML file. It provides an easy format to define different services (containers) with\ndeployment and runtime attributes.\n4.I A REST API is the most popular interface for data exchange for microservices, but\nnot the only one. Microservices can also use RPC and events-based protocols for\ndata exchange.",
